nux 9.6) using mariadb-server-galera + galera + mariadb-backup. Fixed two environment issues along the way: wsrep_provider path (galera-4 -> galera) and an SELinux AVC denial blocking mariabackup's connectto on the mysqld unix socket (resolved with a scoped semodule policy allowing mysqld_t->mysqld_t unix_stream_socket connectto). Firewall ports 3306/4567/4568/4444 opened on all nodes. Verified multi-master write propagation (writes from any node visible on the others), availability during a single-node outage (2/3 quorum, writes continued), and automatic resync of the rejoining node (SST/IST caught it up to full row set, wsrep_local_state=Synced). Completed mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured boot_id + cluster health baseline on all 3 nodes, restarted node1, node2, then node3 sequentially (one at a time, quorum preserved throughout), confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and confirmed each rejoined with wsrep_cluster_size=3, state=Synced, wsrep_ready=ON, and full data (5/5 rows) after each restart. Final state: all 3 nodes synced, cluster_size=3, data consistent everywhere. Credentials (SST user password, appuser password) were generated on-node and passed only via secret_env, never printed after initial generation.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected OS/image on node1-3 (AlmaLinux 9.6) and available packages\",\"Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-backup, galera, mariadb-server-galera on all 3 nodes\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306/4567(tcp+udp)/4568/4444 on all 3 nodes\",\"Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf per node with wsrep_cluster_address, node-specific address/name, wsrep_sst_auth\",\"Diagnosed and fixed wsrep_provider library path (galera-4 -> galera)\",\"Diagnosed SELinux AVC denial (connectto on mysqld unix socket) and installed a scoped semodule policy fix on all 3 nodes\",\"Bootstrapped Galera cluster on node1 via galera_new_cluster\",\"Created sst replication user and appuser test user/testdb\",\"Joined node2 and node3 to the cluster via SST (cleared stale partial datadir on node2 first)\",\"Enabled mariadb.service for boot persistence on all 3 nodes\",\"Verified multi-master write propagation across all 3 nodes\",\"Stopped node3, verified 2/3 quorum and continued writes, restarted node3 and verified automatic resync with data intact\",\"Captured boot_id + cluster health baseline on all nodes\",\"Sequentially restarted node1, node2, node3 (one at a time), verified boot_id changed and cluster re-synced with data intact after each\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Galera cluster formed with 3 members, writes visible from any member\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-52b74cb966564f98\",\"cmd-e0bc0bfc5e5f4010\",\"cmd-b64fbbb20c35463d\",\"cmd-0739cf9b6a384e90\",\"cmd-c297f20b66c04259\",\"cmd-84a3ff068c844444\",\"cmd-2753740e87bf427a\"],\"summary\":\"Cluster bootstrapped on node1, node2 and node3 joined via SST; wsrep_cluster_size=3; a write on node1 and inserts on node2/node3 were all visible on node2 and node3 (SELECT showing all 3 rows)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster stays available when one member is unavailable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6ad5348509eb476d\",\"cmd-01e2454c73b94a13\",\"cmd-df08659aa00a484f\",\"cmd-b5aaa20df9ea4d16\",\"cmd-90e5330c4837474f\"],\"summary\":\"node3 stopped; node1 showed wsrep_cluster_size=2 wsrep_cluster_status=Primary (quorum held); writes via node1 and node2 succeeded and were visible on node2 while node3 was down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Unavailable member resynchronizes automatically on return\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-509ce2dbac4f45a4\",\"cmd-d27e33b488f743e0\"],\"summary\":\"node3 restarted mariadb; wsrep_cluster_size returned to 3, wsrep_local_state_comment=Synced, and SELECT on node3 showed all rows written while it was down, including those from node1 and node2\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-49167eb85a3b42df\",\"cmd-ced63eab48a74534\",\"cmd-1dff9fd322874fea\",\"cmd-152dd9d489814433\",\"cmd-323536c9509a4e60\",\"cmd-720d37df1aad4c2a\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id c207ab79...; reboot acknowledged; connection timed out confirming disconnection; new boot_id 14fa1a6c... proves restart; post-restart wsrep_cluster_size=3 Synced wsrep_ready=ON and 5/5 rows present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8a61c67a592c4115\",\"cmd-dbf30afc13ec4017\",\"cmd-53de45dec33e4d48\",\"cmd-98711d285e254df7\",\"cmd-6344eef2f5f64a71\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id d6298ced...; reboot acknowledged; timeout confirms disconnection; new boot_id 6e0ecc1d... proves restart; post-restart wsrep_cluster_size=3 Synced wsrep_ready=ON and 5/5 rows present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-971a35655c1043e1\",\"cmd-daef4b6f356a45bf\",\"cmd-b4a9fad52c5c4523\",\"cmd-28b33cc99729439d\",\"cmd-fa4e16bbea404cae\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id c2ffc729...; reboot acknowledged; timeout confirms disconnection; new boot_id 4fcdacad... proves restart; post-restart wsrep_cluster_size=3 Synced wsrep_ready=ON and 5/5 rows present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final full-cluster health and data consistency after all restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-89872176160e488b\"],\"summary\":\"wsrep_cluster_size=3, all 3 incoming addresses present, and full 5-row dataset consistent on node1 after all three sequential restarts\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-member MariaDB 10.5 Galera cluster (node1/node2/node3, AlmaLinux 9.6) using mariadb-server-galera + galera + mariadb-backup. Fixed two environment issues along the way: wsrep_provider path (galera-4 -> galera) and an SELinux AVC denial blocking mariabackup's connectto on the mysqld unix socket (resolved with a scoped semodule policy allowing mysqld_t->mysqld_t unix_stream_socket connectto). Firewall ports 3306/4567/4568/4444 opened on all nodes. Verified multi-master write propagation (writes from any node visible on the others), availability during a single-node outage (2/3 quorum, writes continued), and automatic resync of the rejoining node (SST/IST caught it up to full row set, wsrep_local_state=Synced). Completed mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured boot_id + cluster health baseline on all 3 nodes, restarted node1, node2, then node3 sequentially (one at a time, quorum preserved throughout), confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and confirmed each rejoined with wsrep_cluster_size=3, state=Synced, wsrep_ready=ON, and full data (5/5 rows) after each restart. Final state: all 3 nodes synced, cluster_size=3, data consistent everywhere. Credentials (SST user password, appuser password) were generated on-node and passed only via secret_env, never printed after initial generation.","actions_performed":["Inspected OS/image on node1-3 (AlmaLinux 9.6) and available packages","Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-backup, galera, mariadb-server-galera on all 3 nodes","Opened firewalld ports 3306/4567(tcp+udp)/4568/4444 on all 3 nodes","Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf per node with wsrep_cluster_address, node-specific address/name, wsrep_sst_auth","Diagnosed and fixed wsrep_provider library path (galera-4 -> galera)","Diagnosed SELinux AVC denial (connectto on mysqld unix socket) and installed a scoped semodule policy fix on all 3 nodes","Bootstrapped Galera cluster on node1 via galera_new_cluster","Created sst replication user and appuser test user/testdb","Joined node2 and node3 to the cluster via SST (cleared stale partial datadir on node2 first)","Enabled mariadb.service for boot persistence on all 3 nodes","Verified multi-master write propagation across all 3 nodes","Stopped node3, verified 2/3 quorum and continued writes, restarted node3 and verified automatic resync with data intact","Captured boot_id + cluster health baseline on all nodes","Sequentially restarted node1, node2, node3 (one at a time), verified boot_id changed and cluster re-synced with data intact after each"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Galera cluster formed with 3 members, writes visible from any member","command_ids":["cmd-52b74cb966564f98","cmd-e0bc0bfc5e5f4010","cmd-b64fbbb20c35463d","cmd-0739cf9b6a384e90","cmd-c297f20b66c04259","cmd-84a3ff068c844444","cmd-2753740e87bf427a"],"summary":"Cluster bootstrapped on node1, node2 and node3 joined via SST; wsrep_cluster_size=3; a write on node1 and inserts on node2/node3 were all visible on node2 and node3 (SELECT showing all 3 rows)"},{"requirement":"Cluster stays available when one member is unavailable","command_ids":["cmd-6ad5348509eb476d","cmd-01e2454c73b94a13","cmd-df08659aa00a484f","cmd-b5aaa20df9ea4d16","cmd-90e5330c4837474f"],"summary":"node3 stopped; node1 showed wsrep_cluster_size=2 wsrep_cluster_status=Primary (quorum held); writes via node1 and node2 succeeded and were visible on node2 while node3 was down"},{"requirement":"Unavailable member resynchronizes automatically on return","command_ids":["cmd-509ce2dbac4f45a4","cmd-d27e33b488f743e0"],"summary":"node3 restarted mariadb; wsrep_cluster_size returned to 3, wsrep_local_state_comment=Synced, and SELECT on node3 showed all rows written while it was down, including those from node1 and node2"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-49167eb85a3b42df","cmd-ced63eab48a74534","cmd-1dff9fd322874fea","cmd-152dd9d489814433","cmd-323536c9509a4e60","cmd-720d37df1aad4c2a"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id c207ab79...; reboot acknowledged; connection timed out confirming disconnection; new boot_id 14fa1a6c... proves restart; post-restart wsrep_cluster_size=3 Synced wsrep_ready=ON and 5/5 rows present"},{"requirement":"Node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-8a61c67a592c4115","cmd-dbf30afc13ec4017","cmd-53de45dec33e4d48","cmd-98711d285e25